# Her own books in Russian: свой, своя, своих
subtitle: "Свою or её? Russian свой, своя, свои in every case: the subject's own, and when it is someone else's."
tags: ["russian","свой","russian possessives","его её свой","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/possessive-svoi"]
thumb: "band \"Her own books, in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Getting married in Russian: выйти замуж, жениться","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/178-russian-getting-married.cast"}

